      \approx6\!-\!7\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy}\approx0.6\!-\!0.7\ {\rm mGy}
\end{equation*}

per 33 keV fan scan, $\approx0.64\,{\rm mGy}$ with $W/e=33.85\,{\rm V}$,
i.e. $D_{1}\approx3.9\,\mu{\rm Gy}$ per dwell is the conventional
single–projection, single–pixel surface dose normally quoted for the
system.  The $0.19\,{\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}$ peak rate is the dose rate in the
$0.30\times6\,{\rm mm^{2}}$ focal spot. ∎

4.text:
For an air walled chamber the power which is put into the air which is
instantaneously in the $w_{f}\times h_{f}$ pencil is the ionisation power

\begin{equation*}
\dot E_{a}=I\,W_{a}/e\qquad W_{a}/e\simeq 33.97\;{\rm V}
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
\dot E_{a}=2.0\times10^{-12}\times33.97\approx6.8\times10^{-11}\ {\rm W}
\end{equation*}
in the air which is intersected by the focal spot.  At the focus

\begin{equation*}
A_{f}=w_{f}h_{f}=0.30\,{\rm mm}\times6.0\,{\rm mm}=1.8\times10^{-2}
{\rm cm^{2}},\qquad 
V_{f}=A_{f}L=0.018\times15.1=0.272\ {\rm cm^{3}}
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
m_{a}=\rho_{a}V_{f}=1.293\times10^{-3}{\rm g\,cm^{-3}}\times0.272
{\rm cm^{3}}\approx3.5\times10^{-4}{\rm g}=3.5\times10^{-7}{\rm kg}
\end{equation*}
is the mass of air which is irradiated at the peak of the scan so that
the peak air kerma rate in the $0.30\times6.0\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ microbeam is

\begin{equation*}
\dot K_{a}= \frac{\dot E_{a}}{m_{a}}=\frac{I\,W/e}{\rho_{a}A_{f}L}
        \approx\frac{6.8\times10^{-11}}{3.5\times10^{-7}}
        \approx1.9\!-\!2.0\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy\,s^{-1}}
\end{equation*}

i.e. $\dot K_{a}\simeq0.19\;{\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}$ in air in the focal spot.
With $(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{t}\simeq(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{a}=0.328\;{\rm
cm^{2}g^{-1}}$ at 33 keV

\begin{equation*}
\dot D_{t}\simeq\dot K_{a}\approx1.9\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy\,s^{-1}},\qquad
\dot\Phi\approx\frac{\dot K_{a}}{E(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{a}}\approx
1.1\times10^{8}\ {\rm ph\,cm^{-2}s^{-1}}
\end{equation*}
in the $0.30\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ pencil.  The $50\,{\rm mm}\to0.30\,{\rm
mm}$ horizontal demagnification of the Laue fan is already contained in
the measured $2.0\;{\rm pA}$ focal current.

A material point stays in the $w_{f}=0.30\;{\rm mm}$ wide pencil for the
quoted dwell

\begin{equation*}
t_{d}=w_{f}/v_{s}\equiv w_{f}/({\rm step/exposure})\approx0.020\ {\rm s},
\end{equation*}
so that the kerma actually received by a surface element on one
monochromatic Laue pass is

\begin{equation*}
D_{1}= \dot K_{t}t_{d}\approx1.93\times10^{-4}\times2.0\times10^{-2}
     \approx3.6\!-\!4.0\times10^{-6}\ {\rm Gy}
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
D_{1}\approx3.8\!-\!3.9\;\mu{\rm Gy}\approx4\;\mu{\rm Gy}
\end{equation*}
per 33 keV, 20 ms dwell in the peak of the profile, i.e. $0.19\;{\rm
mGy\,s^{-1}}$ instantaneous in the $0.30\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ spot,
$\approx2.2\times10^{10}{\rm ph\,cm^{-2}}$ per dwell.  This is the
conventional $\sim\mu{\rm Gy}$ synchrotron micro-beam entrance dose
per Laue energy.

The doses add incoherently with energy.  For the normal $N_{E}$-energy
acquisition

\begin{equation*}
D_{N}\simeq N_{E}D_{1},
\end{equation*}
e.g. the canonical dual-energy K-edge set

\begin{equation*}
D_{2}\simeq2D_{1}\approx7\!-\!8\times10^{-6}\ {\rm Gy}\approx7.8\;\mu{\rm Gy}
\end{equation*}
per imaged surface element, $\approx3.9\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per individual
Laue energy, and

\begin{equation*}
D_{3}\simeq3D_{1}\approx1.1\!-\!1.2\times10^{-5}\ {\rm Gy}\approx
10\!-\!12\;\mu{\rm Gy}
\end{equation*}
for the usual three-energy K-edge subtraction set.  This is the
$\sim4\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per energy, $\sim8\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ cumulative
dual-energy surface dose normally quoted for the system.

On a field averaged basis the whole $W_{0}=50\;{\rm mm}$ Laue fan
contains

\begin{equation*}
N_{p}\simeq\frac{W_{0}}{w_{f}}\approx\frac{50}{0.30}\approx1.67\times10^{2}
\end{equation*}
essentially independent channels.  The kerma integrated over the
complete $50\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ fan for one monochromator energy is

\begin{equation*}
K_{\rm fan}\simeq N_{p}D_{1}\approx1.67\times10^{2}\times3.9\times10^{-6}
       \approx6\!-\!7\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy}\approx0.6\!-\!0.7\ {\rm mGy}
\end{equation*}
per single-energy fan scan, $\approx1.2\!-\!1.3\;{\rm mGy}$ for a
dual-energy acquisition, the $3.9\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per 0.02 s dwell being
the peak per-pixel, per-energy surface dose quoted above.  The
$10^{3}$ low nGy estimates obtained with $\rho_{a}=1.293\;{\rm g\,cm^{-3}}$
instead of $1.293\;{\rm mg\,cm^{-3}}$ are the well known mass-unit
error. ∎

