18.text:
In Bragg–Gray the ionisation power which is at any instant in the
$w_{f}\times h_{f}$ pencil which is in the chamber is

\begin{equation*}
\dot E_{a}=I\,W/e\;, \qquad W/e\simeq 33.97\;{\rm V}
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
\dot E_{a}=2.0\times10^{-12}\times33.97\simeq6.8\times10^{-11}\ {\rm W}
\end{equation*}

at 33 keV.  At the focus

\begin{equation*}
A_{f}=w_{f}h_{f}=0.30\,{\rm mm}\times6.0\,{\rm mm}=1.8\times10^{-2}\;{\rm
cm^{2}}
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
V_{f}=A_{f}L=0.018\times15.1=0.272\;{\rm cm^{3}}
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
m_{a}=\rho_{a}V_{f}=1.293\times10^{-3}{\rm g\,cm^{-3}}\times0.272
      \simeq3.5\times10^{-4}{\rm g}=3.5\times10^{-7}{\rm kg}
\end{equation*}

is the mass of air which is irradiated at any instant.  Hence the peak
air kerma rate in the $0.30\times6.0\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ micro-beam is

\begin{equation*}
\dot K_{a}= \frac{\dot E_{a}}{m_{a}}=
\frac{I\,W/e}{\rho_{a}A_{f}L}
\simeq\frac{6.8\times10^{-11}}{3.52\times10^{-7}}
\simeq1.9\!-\!2.0\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy\,s^{-1}}\approx0.19\ {\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}
\end{equation*}

in air at the focus.  With

\begin{equation*}
\left(\mu_{en}/\rho\right)_{t}\simeq\left(\mu_{en}/\rho\right)_{a}
=0.328\;{\rm cm^{2}g^{-1}}
\end{equation*}

at 33 keV

\begin{equation*}
\dot K_{t}\simeq\dot K_{a}\simeq1.9\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy\,s^{-1}},
\qquad 
\dot\Phi\simeq\frac{\dot K_{a}}{E(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{a}}\simeq1.1\times10^{8}
\;{\rm ph\,cm^{-2}s^{-1}}
\end{equation*}

in the $0.30\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ spot.  The $50\,{\rm mm}\to0.30\,{\rm mm}$
horizontal demagnification of the Laue fan is already contained in the
measured $2.0\;{\rm pA}$ focal current.

A surface element stays in the $w_{f}=0.30\;{\rm mm}$ pencil for the
quoted raster dwell

\begin{equation*}
t_{d}=w_{f}/v_{s}\simeq0.020\;{\rm s},
\end{equation*}

so that the kerma actually booked to a material point on one
monochromatic Laue pass is the per-energy, per-pixel building block

\begin{equation*}
D_{1}= \dot K_{t}t_{d}\simeq1.93\times10^{-4}\times2.0\times10^{-2}
     \simeq3.6\!-\!4.0\times10^{-6}\ {\rm Gy}\approx3.9\;\mu{\rm Gy}
\end{equation*}

per 33 keV, 20 ms dwell in the peak of the profile, i.e.
$0.19\;{\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}\times0.02\;{\rm s}\approx2.2\times10^{10}\;
{\rm ph\,cm^{-2}}$ per dwell.  With $(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{t}\simeq
(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{a}$ this is the entrance absorbed surface dose in soft
tissue for one Laue energy, the conventional $\sim4\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per
energy synchrotron $\mu$-beam figure.

The different Laue energies add incoherently on the same surface point,

\begin{equation*}
D_{N}\simeq N_{E}D_{1},
\end{equation*}

so that the dose actually deposited by a multiple-energy acquisition at
the same raster point is the $N_{E}$-fold sum.  For the canonical
dual-energy K-edge / material decomposition set $N_{E}=2$,

\begin{equation*}
D_{2}\simeq2D_{1}\approx2\times3.9\times10^{-6}{\rm Gy}
      \approx7\!-\!8\times10^{-6}{\rm Gy}\approx7.6\!-\!7.8\;\mu{\rm Gy}
\end{equation*}

per imaged surface element, $\approx3.9\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per individual
33 keV Laue channel.  With $W/e=33.97\;{\rm V}$

\begin{equation*}
D_{2}\approx7.8\times10^{-6}\ {\rm Gy}\;\;{\rm per\;point},
\end{equation*}

i.e. $\sim0.19\;{\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}$ instantaneous in the
$0.30\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ spot and $\sim4\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per energy per
20 ms dwell.  The often quoted three-energy set is

\begin{equation*}
D_{3}\simeq3D_{1}\approx1.1\!-\!1.2\times10^{-5}\ {\rm Gy}\approx
10\!-\!12\;\mu{\rm Gy}\ {\rm per\;point},
\end{equation*}

$\sim4\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per Laue energy.

Field integrated over the whole $W_{0}=50\;{\rm mm}$ monochromator fan

\begin{equation*}
N_{p}=W_{0}/w_{f}\simeq 50/0.30\approx1.67\times10^{2}
\end{equation*}

independent Laue steps make up one complete horizontal raster,
$T_{scan}=N_{p}t_{d}\approx3.33\;{\rm s}$.  The entrance kerma summed
over the whole $50\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ fan for one monochromatic energy
is

\begin{equation*}
K_{\rm fan}\simeq N_{p}D_{1}=\dot K_{t}T_{scan}
          \approx1.67\times10^{2}\times3.9\times10^{-6}
          \approx6\!-\!7\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy}\approx0.6\!-\!0.7\ {\rm mGy}
\end{equation*}

per single-energy complete $50\;{\rm mm}$ scan, $\approx1.2\!-\!1.3\;{\rm mGy}$
for the conventional dual-energy acquisition.  The $3.9\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ per
$0.02\;{\rm s}$ dwell is the peak per-pixel, per-energy surface dose
normally quoted for the system; the $N_{E}$-fold sum $D_{N}=N_{E}D_{1}$,
$\sim7\!-\!8\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ dual, $\sim11\!-\!12\;\mu{\rm Gy}$ triple, is
the cumulative per-point surface dose actually booked to the tissue by
the multiple-energy Laue imager.  This is the $\sim\mu{\rm Gy}$ per point
cumulative level, $ \dot K\approx0.19\;{\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}$ peak in the
$0.30\times6\;{\rm mm^{2}}$ spot, on which the $\sim0.6\!-\!0.7\;{\rm mGy}$
per single-energy fan, $\sim1.2\!-\!1.3\;{\rm mGy}$ dual-energy,
field-integrated numbers are based. ∎

